      "id": 484408,
      "username": "peterg",
      "name": "Peter",
      "created_at": "2025-10-19T06:50:24.485Z",
      "cooked": "<p>wkhtmltopdf is a major pain to work with. If you can avoid it, you probably should.</p>\n<p>I’m not sure what the current status of this roll out is, but Frappe v16 (to be released in the future) and Print Designer (available now) both enable PDF generation via headless chrome. If it were me, I’d pursue one of those two options rather than trying to troubleshoot wkhtmltopdf.</p>\n<p>If you do want to use wkhtmltopdf, it sounds like the issue is with homebrew/apple silicon support. Fixing that is way beyond the scope of what Frappe can do (especially when it’s moving to a new solution anyway).</p>",
